      "description": "Native Cultures of Western North America is a new exhibit which explores the lifeways of dozens of Native American peoples from the Mississippi River to the Pacific Ocean, from Alaska to Mexico. Well-known and respected Arizona businessman Lou Grubb and his wife Evelyn assembled over the course of their lifetimes a marvelous collection of Native American art and material culture. Nearly all the objects in the exhibition are from the Evelyn and Lou Grubb collection; a few objects have been added from AzMNH collections. The museum are extremely grateful to the Grubb family for the donation of the collection.",
